      "review_notes": "The independent target reads a uniformly permuted labelled urn until the requested marked draw, counting preceding unmarked entries. Partitioning the ordering by its first position gives the color recurrence. The CTE proof is finite two-counter induction; the new support continuation supplies positivity of the unmarked population on an actual failure. I suggested merging duplicate first-position expectation wrappers, and the author did so. Tests cover zero requests, no unmarked balls, a one-marked/one-unmarked population with expectation (F 0 + F 1)/2, arbitrary infinite credits, and framed caller resources. Requesting all marked balls does not consume any trailing unmarked balls."
    },
