      "review_notes": "The callback builds one independent success block, whose verified Bernoulli bias is p^n; the existing geometric specification then gives the number of failed blocks. This is a derived composition and does not claim a rolling-window waiting-time law. The public proof needs no uniform-integer assumption. Tests cover block size one, the p=1 zero-failure endpoint, arbitrary infinite credits, and resource framing."
